    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, thanks. Could you expand a bit more on the specific step where the sulfur-containing amino acid sulfoxides are converted into the volatile gas? Also, why is the reaction so sudden? It feels like the moment the knife hits the onion, the eye irritation starts almost instantly. Is there anything about the way the molecules travel or the speed of the breakdown that explains that sudden \"attack\" on the senses?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
