      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The conversion of sulfoxides to volatile gases often involves further oxidation or decomposition catalyzed by other enzymes present in the plant tissue. The reaction is extremely rapid because it is initiated by the physical disruption of cell walls, which suddenly brings the reactants—the enzymes and substrates—into close, high-concentration contact. This instantaneous mixing, coupled with the high reactivity of the sulfur compounds, allows the volatile irritant molecules to immediately vaporize and travel through the air to irritate your eyes.",
      "source": "target",
